{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1521792-spirits-to-humans","id":1521792,"title":"Spirits to Humans","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-31T17:07:46-07:00","id":1521792,"title":"Spirits to Humans","content":"Purely a speculative question, and broad strokes. An Adept of Spirit and Life can -in theory- transform a Spirit into a human. How would a Spirit's psychology react to being human, with their Shadow-ecology imperatives being replaced with actual biology? <br /> And in the event of a Spirit living as a human long enough <i>could</i> develop a functionally human psychology, what impact would it have to be turned back into a Spirit? How deeply would that change them and their nature, if at all?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T17:33:40-07:00","id":1521793,"title":"","content":"The main thing would be that their mentality would chance from predators with alliances due to mutual convenience, to the more pack mentality of humans. Biological functions, like the regular need for sleep would be <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TYT4RKQHRXM\" target=\"_blank\">utterly terrifying</a> to them, with the mounting exhaustion wearing at their mental state until they figure it out by default. The source of their power is widely available, they even sell it at markets and convenience stores, &quot;but you can't take it by just being strong ? Madness&quot;. They would also be disturbed by the fact that they do not have natural combative instincts, or just know the thing they were good at. Actually having too much of that food power source is bad for them, plus they need gadgets and training to be able to fight, very odd, almost as much as the humans not seeing any of that as acceptable. You do not even need to promote your theme or domain, so....what aim do you even have in life ? Which leads me to believe that would make for a very emotionally impactful experience, which would be carved deep into their memory.<br /> <br /> When they revert back into a spirit, the biological imperatives to &quot;succeed and live, fail and be devoured&quot; would come back in full force, but now with a deeper understanding of the human experience. What that means is entirely up to whatever type of person they were. Maybe they were ghouled and now they are much more manipulative. Perhaps they grew fond of someone and now want to make them a Purified, either not to lose them or to have someone to ground them. Maybe they found something they are passionate about and now choose to expand their domain to include that topic, such as a knowledge spirit seeking to become the patron of scriptwriters, due to being impressed by a play organized by Th\u00e9archs to push back the Lie. It all depends on what they took away from the experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T19:25:12-07:00","id":1521797,"title":"","content":"I think a Patterning spell could convert the corpus of a spirit into a human, but wouldn't be able to affect deep seated features like Influence and Essence (and more than I would expect such magic to be able to turn a mage into something incapable of using Awakened magic). I think that sort of thing falls within the remit of appropriate Imperial Practices, the ones that can create (or remove) appropriate magical templates.<br /> <br /> Mind, even if you really were turning a spirit into a genuine article sort of human with no vestiges remaining of their former nature, I think their more immediate issue would be the toll taken by the lack of a soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-07T01:07:45-07:00","id":1522206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1521792-spirits-to-humans?p=1521793#post1521793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They would also be disturbed by the fact that they do not have natural combative instincts, or just know the thing they were good at.</div> </div> </div> </div>Instincts being a purview of Life they may be able to be Patterned in, at least some level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a Patterning spell could convert the corpus of a spirit into a human, but wouldn't be able to affect deep seated features like Influence and Essence (and more than I would expect such magic to be able to turn a mage into something incapable of using Awakened magic). I think that sort of thing falls within the remit of appropriate Imperial Practices, the ones that can create (or remove) appropriate magical templates.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are some limits, like not being able to create a soul, but i am not sure Spirits are as well protected as Player Character templates...<br /> <br /> Yes, turning a Mage into a chair results in an Awakened chair. But you are proposing that a spirit-person would need to eat, sleep, and consume essence (or fall into hibernation?)<br /> <br /> Or possibly after a time learn to either A) convert food into essence or B) repair their body with essence making eating (and maybe sleep) unnecessary?<br /> <br /> Having a spirit-person with influences and human instinct would be an interesting antagonist/ally, especially since they lack a soul, which would be a pretty dead give away.<br /> <br /> But I suspect Patterning should be able to alter these underlying essence/influence based things, in the same way i don't think they would be able to use manifestations with a human body.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-07T10:02:26-07:00","id":1522222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1521792-spirits-to-humans?p=1521793#post1521793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Biological functions, like the regular need for sleep would be <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TYT4RKQHRXM\" target=\"_blank\">utterly terrifying</a> to them, with the mounting exhaustion wearing at their mental state until they figure it out by default.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think spirits have their own forms of instincts to sleep? Not biological, but I recall reading how they tend to become a lot less energetic during the day due to the overwhelming presence of Helios.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}